  "notes": "R.E.A. Holdings plc (Main Market UK, USD reporting). Indonesian palm oil operator (East Kalimantan), ~26,300 ha planted (~65k acres). UK semi-annual reporter (H1 June + FY December). Carries materially more debt than peers (preference shares, $ notes, IDR loans); net debt $169M FY24 vs net cash at AEP/MPE. Stone/coal interest divested 2023. Revenue almost all CPO/PK + small CPKO. Hectares converted via × 2.47. R.E.A. Holdings has Indonesian palm interests since the 1980s; first East Kalimantan estate (PT REA Kaltim) developed from 1989. Pre-2008 reported under UK GAAP in GBP; transitioned to IFRS USD reporting from 2008. Pre-2008 figures restated to USD at average GBP/USD. H1 cadence consistent from inception of modern reporting. Stone/coal segment (Indonesian aggregate) divested 2023. Operating expense breakdown (Cost of sales / Administrative expenses) drawn from consolidated income statement of REA annual reports filed on rea.co.uk IR archive; H1 interim trading updates do not split categories so field omitted there.",
